{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MN4V796429qPwC2t6jcodv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\tpackage format\n5\t\n6\timport (\n7\t\t\"strings\"\n8\t\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n9\t)\n10\t\n11\tconst columnGap = 2\n12\t\n13\t// PadRight pads s with trailing spaces to the given width, measured in runes.\n14\t// R4.1: used for left-aligned column output.\n15\tfunc PadRight(s string, width int) string {\n16\t\tn := utf8.RuneCountInString(s)\n17\t\tif n >= width {\n18\t\t\treturn s\n19\t\t}\n20\t\treturn s + strings.Repeat(\" \", width-n)\n21\t}\n22\t\n23\t// PadLeft pads s with leading spaces to the given width, measured in runes.\n24\t// R4.2: used for right-aligned numeric columns.\n25\tfunc PadLeft(s string, width int) string {\n26\t\tn := utf8.RuneCountInString(s)\n27\t\tif n >= width {\n28\t\t\treturn s\n29\t\t}\n30\t\treturn strings.Repeat(\" \", width-n) + s\n31\t}\n32\t\n33\t// Columns arranges entries into a grid that fits within termWidth columns.\n34\t// R4.3: fills top-to-bottom, left-to-right like GNU ls -C with a 2-space gap.\n35\tfunc Columns(entries []string, termWidth int) [][]string {\n36\t\tif len(entries) == 0 {\n37\t\t\treturn nil\n38\t\t}\n39\t\tnumCols := findMaxColumns(entries, termWidth)\n40\t\treturn buildGrid(entries, numCols)\n41\t}\n42\t\n43\tfunc findMaxColumns(entries []string, termWidth int) int {\n44\t\tn := len(entries)\n45\t\tfor cols := n; cols > 1; cols-- {\n46\t\t\tif gridFits(entries, cols, termWidth) {\n47\t\t\t\treturn cols\n48\t\t\t}\n49\t\t}\n50\t\treturn 1\n51\t}\n52\t\n53\tfunc gridFits(entries []string, cols, termWidth int) bool {\n54\t\trows := (len(entries) + cols - 1) / cols\n55\t\ttotal := 0\n56\t\tfor c := 0; c < cols; c++ {\n57\t\t\tcolWidth := columnWidth(entries, c, rows)\n58\t\t\tif c < cols-1 {\n59\t\t\t\ttotal += colWidth + columnGap\n60\t\t\t} else {\n61\t\t\t\ttotal += colWidth\n62\t\t\t}\n63\t\t\tif total > termWidth {\n64\t\t\t\treturn false\n65\t\t\t}\n66\t\t}\n67\t\treturn true\n68\t}\n69\t\n70\tfunc columnWidth(entries []string, col, rows int) int {\n71\t\tmaxW := 0\n72\t\tfor row := 0; row < rows; row++ {\n73\t\t\tidx := col*rows + row\n74\t\t\tif idx >= len(entries) {\n75\t\t\t\tbreak\n76\t\t\t}\n77\t\t\tw := utf8.RuneCountInString(entries[idx])\n78\t\t\tif w > maxW {\n79\t\t\t\tmaxW = w\n80\t\t\t}\n81\t\t}\n82\t\treturn maxW\n83\t}\n84\t\n85\tfunc buildGrid(entries []string, cols int) [][]string {\n86\t\trows := (len(entries) + cols - 1) / cols\n87\t\tgrid := make([][]string, rows)\n88\t\tfor r := 0; r < rows; r++ {\n89\t\t\trow := make([]string, 0, cols)\n90\t\t\tfor c := 0; c < cols; c++ {\n91\t\t\t\tidx := c*rows + r\n92\t\t\t\tif idx >= len(entries) {\n93\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n94\t\t\t\t}\n95\t\t\t\trow = append(row, entries[idx])\n96\t\t\t}\n97\t\t\tgrid[r] = row\n98\t\t}\n99\t\treturn grid\n100\t}\n101\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_014eHMG7U1Y3u8mbaoLp47db","session_id":"9a1ae14b-d34f-46c6-a4aa-f6d7bfeec2ba","uuid":"85622005-5f1b-4724-9fbb-65f5ce053cee","timestamp":"2026-05-27T20:13:22.435Z"}
