{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014eHMG7U1Y3u8mbaoLp47db","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile my findings.\n\n## Summary: cmd/ls Implementation and pkg/format Architecture\n\nBased on my thorough exploration of the codebase, here are my findings:\n\n---\n\n### **1. cmd/ls/main.go Structure**\n\n**File Path:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5608/cmd/ls/main.go`\n\n**Key Observations:**\n\n- **Does NOT have a shared listing engine for cmd/dir to call.** The implementations are completely independent:\n  - cmd/ls has 44 functions dedicated to ls-specific logic\n  - cmd/dir has 10 functions with its own separate column layout algorithm\n  - They both call sys.TerminalWidth() and sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() but share no listing logic\n\n**Supported Flags:**\n```\n-1             single column output\n-a             show dot files (. and ..)\n-A             show dot files (but not . and ..)\n-C             force column output (default for terminal)\n-d             list directories themselves, not contents\n-F             append indicators (*/=>@|)\n-h             human-readable sizes with -l/-s\n-i             show inode numbers\n-l             long format\n-n             long format with numeric UIDs/GIDs\n-R             recursive\n-r             reverse sort\n-s             show block allocation\n-S             sort by size\n-t             sort by modification time\n-U             unsorted (directory order)\n-v             natural (version) sort\n-x             horizontal column sort (by lines)\n--color[=WHEN] colorize output (always/auto/never)\n--help         show help\n--version      show version\n```\n\n**Core Architecture:**\n\n1. **Options struct** (lines 54-74): Holds all flag states\n2. **Run pipeline** (line 233): Classifies paths → sorts → displays\n3. **Display modes**: Three separate code paths:\n   - Long format (`writeLongFiles`/`writeLongDir`)\n   - Column format (`writeColumnsWidth`/`writeHorizontalColumns`)\n   - Single-column format (`writeLines`)\n4. **Entry building** (`buildDisplayNames`): Optionally adds inode, blocks, color, classification\n5. **Color integration**: Uses `format.FileTypeColor()` and `format.Reset()`\n6. **Terminal handling**: Queries width at startup, registers SIGWINCH handler for updates\n\n---\n\n### **2. pkg/format Capabilities**\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5608/pkg/format/`\n\n**Provides:**\n\n| Component | File | Purpose |\n|-----------|------|---------|\n| **Padding** | `pad.go` | `PadRight()` for left-align, `PadLeft()` for right-align (rune-aware) |\n| **Columns** | `columns.go` (101 lines) | `Columns()` builds grid layout with top-to-bottom fill, 2-space gap |\n| **Colors** | `color.go` | `FileTypeColor()`, `Reset()`, `SetColorEnabled()`, `ColorEnabled()`, `ResetColorEnabled()` |\n| **Human Sizes** | `humansize.go` | `HumanSize()` with binary (1024) or SI (1000) modes, one decimal place |\n| **Alignment** | `align.go` | Empty stub file (only 105 bytes) |\n\n**Color Support:**\n- Directories (blue)\n- Symlinks (cyan)\n- Executables (green)\n- Pipes/FIFOs (yellow on black)\n- Sockets (magenta)\n- Block devices (yellow)\n- Char devices (yellow)\n- Respects `--color=always/auto/never`\n- Thread-safe with RWMutex override mechanism\n\n**Column Algorithm:**\n- Fills top-to-bottom, left-to-right (like GNU ls -C)\n- Dynamically finds max columns that fit terminal width\n- Adds 2-space gap between columns\n- Rune-aware width measurement (handles multibyte UTF-8)\n\n---\n\n### **3. pkg/sys Capabilities**\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5608/pkg/sys/`\n\n**Core Components:**\n\n| Component | File | Purpose |\n|-----------|------|---------|\n| **FileInfo** | `fileinfo.go` | Extended metadata struct with Ino, Blocks, Uid/Gid, ModTime, AccessTime, ChangeTime |\n| **Stat** | `fileinfo.go` | `Stat()` and `Lstat()` wrappers for extended metadata |\n| **Darwin impl** | `stat_darwin.go` | Extracts from `syscall.Stat_t` (handles Mtimespec, Atimespec, Ctimespec) |\n| **Terminal Width** | `terminal.go` | `TerminalWidth()`, `IsTerminal()` via `unix.IoctlGetWinsize(TIOCGWINSZ)` |\n| **Resize Handler** | `signal.go` | `OnTerminalResize()` registers SIGWINCH callbacks, supports multiple callbacks |\n| **SIGPIPE Handler** | `sigpipe.go` | `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - exits 0 on broken pipe (signal.Notify, no signal.Ignore) |\n\n**FileInfo struct fields:**\n```go\nMode       os.FileMode\nSize       int64\nNlink      uint64\nUid/Gid    uint32\nRdev       uint64\nDev        uint64\nIno        uint64\nBlocks     int64\nBlksize    int64\nModTime    time.Time       // modification time\nAccessTime time.Time       // access time (atime)\nChangeTime time.Time       // status change time (ctime)\nInfo       os.FileInfo     // original os.FileInfo\n```\n\n---\n\n### **4. Architecture Summary**\n\n**No Shared Listing Engine:**\n- cmd/ls and cmd/dir are completely independent implementations\n- Both use sys.TerminalWidth() for width queries\n- Both use sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() for pipe handling\n- cmd/ls uses pkg/format extensively (colors, padding, columns, human sizes)\n- cmd/dir implements its own column layout with tab-based indentation\n\n**cmd/ls Uniqueness:**\n- Sophisticated sorting (time, size, version, reverse)\n- Long-format output with permissions, ownership, timestamps\n- Recursive directory traversal with headers\n- Entry classification (/, @, |, =, *)\n- Color-coded output by file type\n- Multiple display modes (1, -C, -x, -l)\n- Total block count output\n- Human-readable size formatting\n\n**pkg/format is Specialized for ls:**\n- Column layout algorithm is specifically tuned for ls -C behavior\n- Color scheme hardcoded for GNU coreutils ls compatibility\n- Padding functions work at rune level (UTF-8 aware)\n- Not designed as a general utility library\n\n---\n\n**Key Files to Reference:**\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5608/cmd/ls/main.go` - Full implementation\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5608/pkg/format/columns.go` - Column layout algorithm\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5608/pkg/sys/fileinfo.go` - Extended metadata wrapper\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5608/cmd/dir/main.go` - Contrast implementation"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a1ae14b-d34f-46c6-a4aa-f6d7bfeec2ba","uuid":"885b9f15-87fb-46af-a787-4330c3110f5d","timestamp":"2026-05-27T20:14:18.700Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5608, I need to understand how cmd/ls is implemented and what pkg/format provides.\n\n1. Check if cmd/ls/main.go exists and read it entirely\n2. Check what files exist under pkg/format/ and read key files\n3. Check what's in pkg/sys/ - especially TerminalWidth and InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n\nI need to understand:\n- Does cmd/ls have a shared listing engine that cmd/dir can call?\n- What flags does cmd/ls support?\n- What does pkg/format provide (column alignment, escaping, etc.)?\n\nSearch breadth: very thorough","agentId":"ab3d4ac0a5c3f09a5","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile my findings.\n\n## Summary: cmd/ls Implementation and pkg/format Architecture\n\nBased on my thorough exploration of the codebase, here are my findings:\n\n---\n\n### **1. cmd/ls/main.go Structure**\n\n**File Path:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5608/cmd/ls/main.go`\n\n**Key Observations:**\n\n- **Does NOT have a shared listing engine for cmd/dir to call.** The implementations are completely independent:\n  - cmd/ls has 44 functions dedicated to ls-specific logic\n  - cmd/dir has 10 functions with its own separate column layout algorithm\n  - They both call sys.TerminalWidth() and sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() but share no listing logic\n\n**Supported Flags:**\n```\n-1             single column output\n-a             show dot files (. and ..)\n-A             show dot files (but not . and ..)\n-C             force column output (default for terminal)\n-d             list directories themselves, not contents\n-F             append indicators (*/=>@|)\n-h             human-readable sizes with -l/-s\n-i             show inode numbers\n-l             long format\n-n             long format with numeric UIDs/GIDs\n-R             recursive\n-r             reverse sort\n-s             show block allocation\n-S             sort by size\n-t             sort by modification time\n-U             unsorted (directory order)\n-v             natural (version) sort\n-x             horizontal column sort (by lines)\n--color[=WHEN] colorize output (always/auto/never)\n--help         show help\n--version      show version\n```\n\n**Core Architecture:**\n\n1. **Options struct** (lines 54-74): Holds all flag states\n2. **Run pipeline** (line 233): Classifies paths → sorts → displays\n3. **Display modes**: Three separate code paths:\n   - Long format (`writeLongFiles`/`writeLongDir`)\n   - Column format (`writeColumnsWidth`/`writeHorizontalColumns`)\n   - Single-column format (`writeLines`)\n4. **Entry building** (`buildDisplayNames`): Optionally adds inode, blocks, color, classification\n5. **Color integration**: Uses `format.FileTypeColor()` and `format.Reset()`\n6. **Terminal handling**: Queries width at startup, registers SIGWINCH handler for updates\n\n---\n\n### **2. pkg/format Capabilities**\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix